[
    {
        "content": "<p>I was able to correctly guess that the goal <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo mathvariant=\"normal\">≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">6 \\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">6</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mord vbox\"><span class=\"thinbox\"><span class=\"rlap\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"inner\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\"></span></span></span><span class=\"fix\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace nobreak\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> could be resolved by the <code>trivial</code> tactic.</p>\n<p>I haven't been able to find a list of what <code>trivial</code> does. I like that there's a <code>simp?</code> that tells you how <code>simp</code> got to its result. It'd be nice if there was a <code>trivial?</code> too, but failing that, is there documentation somewhere that specifies what it can and can't resolve?</p>",
        "id": 611847517,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael",
        "timestamp": 1784626629
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>show_term</code> probably suggests that it used <code>decide</code>.</p>",
        "id": 611852798,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1784628419
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In this case you can just use <code>#print</code> I guess since it's a macro: <a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=C4Cwpg9gTmC2AEBnAlgDwPoDszoF5igngC54A2eQAyJ4AGEgXngCMBPeYKZAN2QEMAbAFCCA9AFpBoSDAQoM2PASKkK1OsUYQAZugAmYAMbJ96MAEd0HAK5h4ACmP2AomYB0MLf3ZQbASl%2BCYiKCAMQADpyYwEhoWDj4hEA\">playground link</a></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">six_ne_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">theorem six_ne_zero : 6 ≠ 0 := of_decide_eq_true (id (Eq.refl true))</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">print</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">six_ne_zero</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 611853657,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Bailey",
        "timestamp": 1784628727
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you go and Ctrl+Click on the tactic you should also get to the <code>macro_rules</code> declaration for the extension to <code>trivial</code> that actually succeeded. In this case you'll get to</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">macro_rules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decide</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 611856388,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1784629715
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the documentation should be at <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/tactics.html#userName-trivial\">tactic#trivial</a></p>",
        "id": 611875374,
